From 9a032eb3ce96a567a3947d42e19a9668594b41dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 22:23:28 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] avcodec/h2645_sei: honor frame-packing persistence

H.264 frame-packing state is currently cleared for every access unit even
when arrangement_repetition_period is non-zero. HEVC parses the same message
but discards arrangement_persistence_flag, leaving its state sticky.

For HEVC, read the persistence flag and apply it after exporting side data
for the current frame.

For H.264 an arrangement lasts until the next message or the end of the
coded video sequence, in output order (H.264 D.2.26). Keep the message
with its picture and resolve the arrangement when the picture is selected
for output, so that a message reaches the pictures output after it even if
they were decoded earlier, a cancellation does not reach the ones output
before it, and nothing survives an IDR picture or a flush. Temporal
interleaving alternates the constituent frames in output order. The state
is copied between frame threads with the other output state.

Export the Stereo 3D side data only there, using ff_decode_stereo3d_new(),
so that side data supplied by the caller or the container is neither
removed nor duplicated and -side_data_prefer_packet is honored.

Add H.264 and HEVC FATE samples covering persistent, cancelled and
current-frame-only arrangements. The H.264 test uses four frame threads to
exercise context propagation.

Suggested-by: Kacper Michajlow (kasper93)
Link: https://github.com/mpv-player/mpv/pull/18490#discussion_r4066349407
Signed-off-by: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet via Claude Code
